+### `withoutQuery(input, keys)`
+
+Removes the given query parameter(s) from the URL.
+
+Other parameters keep their order and their original encoding. If no parameters are left, the `?` is removed as well. Keys are matched after decoding, so an encoded key like `a%20b` matches `a b`.
+
+**Example:**
+
+```js
+withoutQuery("/foo?bar=1&baz=2", "bar"); // "/foo?baz=2"
+withoutQuery("/foo?bar=1&bar=2&baz=3", "bar"); // "/foo?baz=3"
+withoutQuery("/foo?bar=1", "bar"); // "/foo"
+```
+
 ### `withoutTrailingSlash(input, respectQueryAndFragment?)`
 
 Removes the trailing slash from the URL or pathname.
